A||||2||Ted||Head lights||||1||
Z||000000||Ted||01-12-2001||02:23 PM||||I'm sure this might have already been asked before, but my left headlight won't go up or down. The light still works but it doesn't move. I have it up at all times now but I would like it to go up and down on its own. Do I have to buy a new kit for it or what?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DrRodey||01-12-2001||03:09 PM||||Depending on what year Fiero you have it can be as simple as replacing the bushings in the headlight motor (87-88) or if it is the older model (84-86) you would be better off replacing the entire motor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero Fanatic||01-12-2001||05:12 PM||||They run on relays. Go to a wrecking yard and get a different isolation relay. The isolation relay distributes the individual power to the 2 headlight motors. Sometimes the can cause only one headlight to go up and down. My headlight motors are now both bad. I had to hook a toggle switch to the isolation relay to run power to put the headlights up and down. Before they used to go up and down and the motors would still spin and make a grinding sound. There is a conversion process to replace the older system and install the later system that is in later models.<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero Fanatic (edited 01-12-2001).]||||reg||1
